      ],
      "source": "https://delawareriverheritagetrail.org/2021/09/28/borough-of-palmyra/",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town began as a small railroad junction called Texas, named after the 1845 U.S. territory that joined the Union.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://delawareriverheritagetrail.org/2021/09/28/borough-of-palmyra/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Palmyra sits where Pennsauken Creek meets the Delaware River, right at the southern tip of Burlington County.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://delawareriverheritagetrail.org/2021/09/28/borough-of-palmyra/",
